<title>FRANCE: Renault says EMU necessary.</title>
<headline>Renault says EMU necessary.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Renault chairman Louis Schweitzer said in a radio interview on Saturday he was convinced that a single European currency should be created as soon as possible.</p>
<p>&quot;We've chosen to be part of a common market. I'm convinced... that a single European market which does not have a single currency isn't something that can function over the long time,&quot; he told Radio Classique, citing the painful recent effects of currency imbalances in Europe.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm convinced we need to go toward a single currency as quickly as possible and we mustn't miss the January 1, 1999, deadline,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Schweitzer's position puts him at odds with his counterpart at PSA Peugeot Citroen, chairman Jacques Calvet, who argues that Europe is putting the cart before the horse by seeking monetary union ahead of political union.</p>
<p>Both car companies have been badly hurt by currency turmoil in Europe, notably by the Italian lira's weakness relative to the French franc.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
